rtners in burkina faso  and nigeria  from there we move to uganda with scovia  atakini who works for nasseri in uganda  her center will focus on finger millets  and sorghums  and her partners include  tanzania  and kenya  and lastly  michael cipetta at longway university  will lead the center of innovation for  crop improvement for east and southern  africa with a focus being on copy  each center of innovation is unique but  together they create a complementary  team based on their opportunities and  challenges within their regions focused  crops  in research agricultural social and  economic systems  one of the directors of the centers of  innovation  geno kane will speak in this session as  well  looking to the future of the innovation  lab for crop improvement we intend to  continue our efforts to support centers  of innovation priorities  building intellectual and operational  capacities in country a continual  development and deployment of scientific  insights tools technologies and methods  we intend to integrate cross-cutting  themes  including gender  youth equity engagement resilience in  all our trainings of all aspects of our  programs and lastly i'd like to spend a  few minutes on identifying establishing  new partnerships  first of all we intend to link with  minority serving institutions in the  united states  and i'm pleased to announce the addition  of dr lavonne esters at purdue to lead  our initiative connecting the innovation  lab with minority serving institutions  we also intend to integrate with seed  systems delivery  i'm also pleased to announce the  addition of seed systems group  led by joe devries most recently having  worked with the alliance for green  revolution in africa to focus on seed  systems activities in haiti and senegal  we also intend to build collaboratively  with private sector partners this  engagement will include in-country focus  ranging from seed companies through  computational slash it groups  for more detailed information on our  innovation lab activities go to  ilc.cornell.edu  as session moderator i'd now like to  introduce our speakers first deborah  rubin co-director of cultural practices  llc  matthew abraham assistant director of  tata cornell institute for food and  agriculture at cornell  kelly robinson assistant professor in  the school of integrative plant sciences  the section of plant breeding and  genetics at cornell  and jedo kane group leader and molecular  biologist for isra of cross in senegal  they will make their presentations  you will  provide questions for the speakers in  the chat box and following all the  presentations we'll have a session where  all the questions are addressed  thanks for your time and i'm looking  forward to a great session thank you
 

